## Minor note (parity, low impact)
`FeedbackQueueModels.swift:261` — `prettyJSON` pretty-prints with `.sortedKeys`, so the `recent_errors` disclosure renders object keys alphabetized (e.g. `line, message, source`), whereas the web `JSON.stringify(recent_errors, null, 2)` preserves source order (`message, source, line`). Dropping `.sortedKeys` restores byte-for-byte parity of that rendered block. Cosmetic, but it's a concrete rendered-string difference.

